  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404410",
      "title": "Adding Validation",
      "lectureOrder": 156,
      "videoOrder": 152,
      "sourceHash": "729e0fe3d850cb847115d84974e2b6b375d0dcd8d7b7444b89b03f8fe317f47f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 5.13,
          "en": "So let's now add validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.13,
          "end": 7,
          "en": "Validation simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7,
          "end": 11.72,
          "en": "that we want to check the entered values before we use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.72,
          "end": 13.9,
          "en": "Now we could add validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.9,
          "end": 17.57,
          "en": "that validates the user input with every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.57,
          "end": 21.21,
          "en": "We could do that, but that is not what I wanna do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.21,
          "end": 23.25,
          "en": "Instead I wanna add validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.25,
          "end": 25.13,
          "en": "that validates the user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.13,
          "end": 27.6,
          "en": "once the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 29.21,
          "en": "So here in submitHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.21,
          "end": 33.7,
          "en": "before we forward the collected data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.7,
          "end": 34.91,
          "en": "I wanna validate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.91,
          "end": 37.81,
          "en": "And if it's incorrect, we won't forward it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.81,
          "end": 39.8,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna show an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.8,
          "end": 41.963,
          "en": "We wanna give the user some feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.18,
          "end": 45.77,
          "en": "So how can we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.77,
          "end": 48.85,
          "en": "Well, we can add a couple of helper constants here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.85,
          "end": 50.947,
          "en": "to make the code a bit more readable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.947,
          "end": 55.583,
          "en": "for determining whether those individual inputs are valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.57,
          "end": 59.26,
          "en": "I will name the first one amountIsValid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.26,
          "end": 63.607,
          "en": "and that should hold true if expenseData.amount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.54,
          "end": 69.15,
          "en": "So this amount converted to a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.15,
          "end": 72.31,
          "en": "is let's say greater than zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.31,
          "end": 75.83,
          "en": "because the amount entered should be greater than zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.83,
          "end": 78.39,
          "en": "to be valid I would argue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 81.28,
          "en": "and I wanna make sure that it's a number in the first place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.28,
          "end": 85.06,
          "en": "So I will make sure that it's not, not a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.06,
          "end": 87.71000000000001,
          "en": "With that built-in is not a number function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.71000000000001,
          "end": 90.3,
          "en": "I pass expenseData.amount to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.3,
          "end": 92.923,
          "en": "And then I combine these two conditions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.02000000000001,
          "end": 97.7,
          "en": "So if it is not a number, if this would be true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.7,
          "end": 99.59,
          "en": "or if it is an amount smaller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.59,
          "end": 101.25,
          "en": "or equal than zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.25,
          "end": 103.86,
          "en": "this would hold false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.86,
          "end": 106.13,
          "en": "If it's not, not a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.13,
          "end": 108.2,
          "en": "and it is greater than zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.2,
          "end": 109.233,
          "en": "it is valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.53999999999999,
          "end": 111.52000000000001,
          "en": "Now for the date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.52000000000001,
          "end": 114.77000000000001,
          "en": "I will also add a dateIsValid, constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.77000000000001,
          "end": 116.50999999999999,
          "en": "and the date should be valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.50999999999999,
          "end": 120.053,
          "en": "if we could successfully convert it to such a date object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.29,
          "end": 123.51,
          "en": "Now, to find out if that worked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.51,
          "end": 126.56,
          "en": "there is an approach that looks a bit strange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.56,
          "end": 128.8,
          "en": "but works really well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 128.8,
          "end": 130.61,
          "en": "And to understand this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.61,
          "end": 133.04,
          "en": "I'll go to the browser and open the dev tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.04,
          "end": 135.15,
          "en": "just so that I can show you something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.15,
          "end": 136.853,
          "en": "in regular JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.36,
          "end": 141.68,
          "en": "Imagine that you create a new date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.68,
          "end": 145.45,
          "en": "and through this constructor you pass a valid date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.45,
          "end": 147.57,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.57,
          "end": 149.943,
          "en": "In that case, we get a valid date object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.32,
          "end": 155.25,
          "en": "Now, if you do pass something invalid, like, hello",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.43,
          "end": 160.19299999999998,
          "en": "you get invalid date as a text output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.11,
          "end": 166.01,
          "en": "You get that if you call toString on that created date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.01,
          "end": 169.563,
          "en": "then you get invalid Date written like this as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.71,
          "end": 172.71,
          "en": "We can utilize this fact here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.71,
          "end": 177.71,
          "en": "and simply check if expenseData.date.toString()",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.09,
          "end": 184.04,
          "en": "is equal to Invalid Date written like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.04,
          "end": 186.09,
          "en": "and make sure you got the casing correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.12,
          "end": 189.2,
          "en": "If this is the case we know it's invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.2,
          "end": 191.79,
          "en": "since I wanna store true here if it is valid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.79,
          "end": 194.32,
          "en": "I need to check for the opposite though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.32,
          "end": 197.67000000000002,
          "en": "So now this will be true if this is not Invalid Date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.67000000000002,
          "end": 201.05,
          "en": "So if it is valid, if it is Invalid Date though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.05,
          "end": 205.203,
          "en": "dateIsValid will store false as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.65,
          "end": 210.7,
          "en": "Now for the description, we can add descriptionIsValid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.7,
          "end": 215.38,
          "en": "and that should be valid if expenseData.description,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.38,
          "end": 217.03,
          "en": "once we trim it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.03,
          "end": 220.48,
          "en": "so once we remove excess wide space at the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.48,
          "end": 224.78,
          "en": "or end of the string has a length, that's greater than zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.78,
          "end": 226.26,
          "en": "So it's not empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.26,
          "end": 229.42000000000002,
          "en": "This allows us to check that the description is not empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.42000000000002,
          "end": 232.083,
          "en": "which is the only validation I wanna perform here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 233.02,
          "end": 236.1,
          "en": "Now we got those three helper constants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.1,
          "end": 238.553,
          "en": "We can now add a if check where we use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.45,
          "end": 243.799,
          "en": "I want to submit if amountIsValid, dateIsValid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 243.799,
          "end": 246.91,
          "en": "and descriptionIsValid is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.91,
          "end": 251.35,
          "en": "That means that I wanna stop and I don't wanna continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 251.35,
          "end": 253.51,
          "en": "if one of them is not true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.51,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "If the others are true, but one of them isn't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 258.683,
          "en": "that's enough for me to stop the submission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 259.59,
          "end": 262.53,
          "en": "So here I will check if not amountIsValid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 265.63,
          "en": "or not dateIsValid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 265.63,
          "end": 267.883,
          "en": "or not descriptionIsValid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 268.82,
          "end": 271.72,
          "en": "If one of these three scenarios is the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 271.72,
          "end": 274.15999999999997,
          "en": "then I wanna return here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 274.15999999999997,
          "end": 277.49,
          "en": "so that this line of code isn't executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.49,
          "end": 280.483,
          "en": "We return and therefore we stop the function execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 281.33,
          "end": 285.14,
          "en": "In addition, I wanna show some feedback to the user here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.14,
          "end": 288.163,
          "en": "to inform the user that the validation failed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 289.07,
          "end": 293.39,
          "en": "For a start we could do this with the Alert API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.39,
          "end": 297.11,
          "en": "From React Native, we can import Alert,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.11,
          "end": 299.61,
          "en": "and we used that before in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.61,
          "end": 301.96,
          "en": "And we could use that to show an alert",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.96,
          "end": 304.853,
          "en": "where we say Invalid input as a title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 305.75,
          "end": 309.46,
          "en": "Please check your input values as a text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.46,
          "end": 311.38,
          "en": "And we could then also configure a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.38,
          "end": 312.87,
          "en": "if we wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 312.87,
          "end": 314.78,
          "en": "Otherwise we'll use the default button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 314.78,
          "end": 316.373,
          "en": "that is provided to us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 317.43,
          "end": 320.94,
          "en": "With this logic added if we saved it all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 320.94,
          "end": 322.17,
          "en": "and reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 323.51,
          "end": 326.913,
          "en": "if we try to submit an empty form, we get this alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 328.12,
          "end": 332.32,
          "en": "If I enter a negative amount here, I get this alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 332.32,
          "end": 335.46,
          "en": "So even if the rest should be valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.46,
          "end": 337.27,
          "en": "if I enter valid data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 337.27,
          "end": 340.28,
          "en": "I get an alert because the amount is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.28,
          "end": 342.08,
          "en": "The same is true if I enter hello here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 342.08,
          "end": 344.93,
          "en": "because this can't be converted to a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 344.93,
          "end": 347.53,
          "en": "If everything is correct though, we can submit this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 348.58,
          "end": 350.9,
          "en": "We can also check the upper inputs here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 350.9,
          "end": 353.22,
          "en": "If the amount is correct,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 353.22,
          "end": 354.6,
          "en": "and the description is correct,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.6,
          "end": 355.83,
          "en": "but the date is empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 355.83,
          "end": 357.56,
          "en": "we get this alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 357.56,
          "end": 361.447,
          "en": "And if I enter something like 2021-1-1,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 365.25,
          "end": 367.11,
          "en": "I also get this alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 367.11,
          "end": 368.32,
          "en": "So that works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 368.32,
          "end": 371.03,
          "en": "if I do enter a correct value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 371.03,
          "end": 372.58,
          "en": "but I leave the description empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 372.58,
          "end": 374.35,
          "en": "I get an alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 374.35,
          "end": 376.46,
          "en": "And if I add a bunch of blanks in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 376.46,
          "end": 377.63,
          "en": "I also get this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 377.63,
          "end": 380.42,
          "en": "because the trim method that we added in our checker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 380.42,
          "end": 381.423,
          "en": "removes those.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 382.59,
          "end": 384.02,
          "en": "So that works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 384.02,
          "end": 386.66,
          "en": "but I actually don't wanna use this alert here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 386.66,
          "end": 387.55,
          "en": "for the feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 387.55,
          "end": 388.72,
          "en": "We could use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 388.72,
          "end": 392.27,
          "en": "but I wanna show you how we can provide feedback to the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 392.27,
          "end": 396.063,
          "en": "directly inside of this user interface here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
